  "notes": "{植|う}え{替|か}え refers to moving a plant to a new pot or location, typically to promote better growth.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {植|う}え{替|か}えをする: to do repotting\n- {植|う}え{替|か}える: to repot (verb form)\n- {植|う}え{替|か}えの{時期|じき}: repotting season\n\nWHEN TO REPOT:\n- {根詰|ねづ}まり: root-bound condition\n- {鉢|はち}が{小|ちい}さくなった: pot has become too small\n- {土|つち}が{古|ふる}くなった: soil has become old/depleted\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {移植|いしょく}: transplanting (more formal/technical; also used for organ transplants)\n- {定植|ていしょく}: permanent planting (from seedbed to final location)\n\nSpring is the most common time for {植|う}え{替|か}え, as plants recover more easily during the growing season.",
